          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Five-try Will Joseph tipped to keep England wing against All Blacks",
          "body": "Gloucester wing Will Joseph was understood, in a BBC report on 16 November, to be in pole position for Saturday's Nations Championship test against New Zealand, with Immanuel Feyi-Waboso ruled out of the autumn by an ankle injury. Joseph's five tries in the 78-15 win over Japan, including a hat-trick inside 19 minutes, made him only the fifth England men's player to score five in one match. Cadan Murley is the squad's other specialist wing. \"He floats, doesn't he?\" said England team-mate Ben Earl."
