          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Ireland captain Dan Sheehan tipped to start at No. 8 against Springboks",
          "body": "According to The 42, Ireland head coach Andy Farrell is expected to move his captain from hooker to the back of the scrum for Saturday's test against South Africa, with Caelan Doris, Jack Conan and Sean Jansen all unavailable. Sheehan, back from the concussion that kept him out of the 43-15 win over Fiji, has never started a test at No. 8 but impressed there for Leinster against Munster in the URC last month. The switch would free Rónan Kelleher to start at hooker between Andrew Porter and Tadhg Furlong."
