          "heading": "Steve Tandy drops All Blacks player of the match Botham against Australia",
          "body": "Wales head coach Steve Tandy has left Cardiff flanker James Botham out of the matchday 23 for Saturday's test against Australia, with Alex Mann starting at blindside. Botham was player of the match in last weekend's 35-28 win over New Zealand, Wales's first against the All Blacks since 1953. His partner is expecting their first child this week, but Tandy insisted that was not part of the selection decision. He said Botham spent Tuesday's training session \"leading the charge, running opposition plays for Australia, and bringing unbelievable intensity.\""
