          "heading": "Les Kiss drops Fraser McReight to bench in five-change Wallabies pack",
          "body": "Fraser McReight, the reigning John Eales Medal winner, drops to the bench with Carlo Tizzano starting at openside as Wallabies coach Les Kiss reshapes the pack for Saturday's Nations Championship Test against Wales. The whole front row is new, with Isaac Kailea, Brandon Paenga-Amosa and Taniela Tupou promoted from the bench, while Tom Hooper makes his first Test start at lock in almost a year, ahead of Jeremy Williams. The backline is untouched from the 12-15 defeat to Scotland, and prop Allan Alaalatoa is in line for a 99th cap as a replacement."
        },
